  "limits": [
    "Redis 8.0.5 ran on WSL on a disposable loopback cluster with three primary shards and one replica.",
    "Three trials. Separate Windows and WSL clients used RESP3/SHARDS for in-flight disconnect and RESP2/SLOTS for unsent admission. Each new write starts after the driver checks surviving Redis slot agreement.",
    "An accepted request can fail with MAY_HAVE_EXECUTED. No application request was replayed after an uncertain result. In this fixture each post-election INCR independently executed once.",
    "One unsent route recreation under the original deadline. A request submitted earlier in an ongoing election can time out or receive no-route.",
    "The observations are loopback recovery timings. Mixed-load failover, black-hole partitions, reintegration, TLS and native production acceptance are open."
  ]
}
